# Template. Copy to `.env` and fill in the key:  cp .env.example .env
#
# One key serves everything: the orchestrator CLI reads ANTHROPIC_API_KEY directly,
# and the backend falls back to it when LEGAL_LENS_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is unset.
# Get a key at https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test the intent classifier — no backend, no database, no frontend:
#
#   cd backend
#   uv run --extra orchestrator python -m legal_lens.orchestrator.cli --suite
#   uv run --extra orchestrator python -m legal_lens.orchestrator.cli "draft a memo on venue"
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run the backend with real generation instead of the deterministic echo stub:
#
#   LEGAL_LENS_LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic uv run uvicorn legal_lens.main:app --reload --port 8000
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run the three-workflow orchestration layer instead: intent routing, a query
# rewrite, hybrid retrieval with a cross-encoder reranker, and a different model and
# effort per workflow. Needs `uv sync --extra workflows` (torch, Qdrant, fastembed:
# minutes, ~2GB).
#
#   LEGAL_LENS_LLM_PROVIDER=orchestrator uv run uvicorn legal_lens.main:app --port 8000
#
# The first question loads two local models (~2.5GB resident) and is slow; the rest
# are not. They load in a worker thread, so nothing else in the service stalls.
#
# Route ask/summary/draft through Haiku rather than the keyword regex. The regex is
# not a placeholder — it mirrors the frontend mock and is what runs under `echo` —
# but it keys on words rather than meaning.
# LEGAL_LENS_INTENT_ROUTER=model
#
# Everything else about the workflows is configured on the `ORCH_` variables the CLI
# reads, so a setting tuned against the eval corpus means the same thing when the
# service runs. The ones worth knowing:
#
# ORCH_WHOLE_DOCUMENT_MAX_TOKENS=120000
#                              # At or below this many tokens in scope, `ask` and
#                              # `draft` read every page and an absence question is
#                              # answerable (FR-13). Above it, hybrid retrieval and
#                              # the reranker. `0` forces always-retrieve, which is
#                              # the configuration the §9.2 reranker measurements
#                              # were taken under — and note that at 120000 a typical
#                              # contract takes the whole-document route, so the
#                              # hybrid pipeline is dormant day to day. Lower it to
#                              # exercise retrieval on realistic corpora.
# ORCH_RERANK_ENABLED=1        # `0` turns the cross-encoder off; read the
#                              # measurements on OrchestratorConfig.rerank_enabled first
# ORCH_ASK_TOP_N=8             # pages reaching an `ask` prompt
# ORCH_DRAFT_TOP_N=12          # wider: a memo cites more ground than an answer
# ORCH_DEVICE=mps              # `mps` on Apple silicon, `cpu` elsewhere
#
# Leave ORCH_RERANK_MIN_SCORE unset unless you have looked at real scores from the
# reranker in use. A floor on a logit-output reranker discards every candidate, and
# the symptom is not an error — it is an assistant that abstains on questions the
# documents plainly answer.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OCR for scanned PDFs. Off by default on purpose: FR-2 requires a scan to be
# rejected rather than transcribed, because a citation into transcribed text quotes
# what the OCR engine produced rather than what the document provably says.
# Needs `uv sync --extra ocr`. Check GET /api/health to confirm it came up.
#
# LEGAL_LENS_OCR_ENABLED=true
#
# Engine: `claude` needs the key above and no system binary. `tesseract` makes no
# vendor call but needs `brew install tesseract`.
# LEGAL_LENS_OCR_ENGINE=claude
#
# LEGAL_LENS_OCR_MAX_PAGES=50
# LEGAL_LENS_OCR_MAX_ILLEGIBLE_RATIO=0.25
